1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:02,019
How does a
civilization survive

2
00:00:02,039 --> 00:00:04,621
where water is worth
more than gold?

3
00:00:04,641 --> 00:00:06,296
In Sarrun,
one cup is a day's

4
00:00:06,316 --> 00:00:07,378
wage.

5
00:00:07,398 --> 00:00:09,685
Houses turn inward,
catching every drop

6
00:00:09,705 --> 00:00:10,682
of dew.

7
00:00:10,702 --> 00:00:11,882
Rations are measured.

8
00:00:11,902 --> 00:00:13,561
Spilling is a crime.

9
00:00:13,581 --> 00:00:15,186
Roads bend from well
to well,

10
00:00:15,206 --> 00:00:16,556
never straight.

11
00:00:16,576 --> 00:00:18,115
And every well is
locked.

12
00:00:18,135 --> 00:00:20,276
One family holds the
keys.

13
00:00:20,296 --> 00:00:22,219
They never needed an
army.

14
00:00:22,399 --> 00:00:24,542
Make anything scarce,
and whoever holds it

15
00:00:24,562 --> 00:00:26,149
rules the region.

16
00:00:26,169 --> 00:00:28,152
Follow for more ways
to turn geography

17
00:00:28,172 --> 00:00:29,789
into storytelling.
